[Round 7/8 | Implementer | 308.8s | 0/400k] The comparison confirms scheduler yields are useful only as a fallback: frequent yields (64 spins/8 yields) materially reduce throughput, while a long bounded spin window keeps the hot path close to the stable implementation. I’m settling on 4096 bounded spin attempts followed by one bounded scheduler yield, which still guarantees periodic yielding under persistent contention without putting `yield_now()` on ordinary short-held lock waits.

