[Round 7/8 | Implementer | 494.7s | 0/400k] A key lock-only result emerged: repeatedly probing the atomic during the spin window caused heavy cache-line traffic. The faster bounded policy does one immediate Acquire CAS, then a bounded `spin_loop` phase without extra atomic probes, then checks/yields in a bounded scheduler-backoff phase before retrying. Native runs are now around 6–8M ops/s, so I’m validating this exact policy at full benchmark duration and then checking correctness.

